            "prompt": {
              "type": "string",
              "label": "abstract_text",
              "value": "METHODS TO REGENERATE UPPER AIRWAY AND DIGESTIVE TRACT TISSUES WITH MICROENERGY ACOUSTIC PULSE OR LOW-INTENSITY PULSED ULTRASOUND. This patent describes microenergy acoustic pulse (MAP) stimulation, a shockwave-based therapy delivered via a probe to muscles of the upper aerodigestive tract (tongue, pharynx, larynx) to treat age-related sarcopenia and myogenic dysfunction disorders including dysphagia (swallowing difficulty), presbyphonia (age-related voice decline), and obstructive sleep apnea. MAP stimulation increases muscle mass and contractility strength, increases the proportion of fast-twitch muscle fibers, reduces numbers of senescent (aged/dysfunctional) cells, and activates the body's own muscle stem cells to regenerate tissue. In sleep apnea, the therapy targets the genioglossus (tongue) and laryngeal muscles to improve the tongue's ability to keep the airway open during sleep. In dysphagia, it targets pharyngeal muscles to restore safe, effective swallowing. In presbyphonia, it targets laryngeal muscles to restore vocal fold strength and voice quality. The shockwave probe delivers energy at 0.033 to 0.05 mJ/mm2, administered in multiple sessions, two or three times per week.",
              "exposedToApp": true
